Spec review verdict: **PASS**.

I compared `fd412468..2356a911` against GitHub issues #15 and #12 and the feature plan. The implementation covers all #15 acceptance criteria in scope:

- durable create precedes completion;
- full-screen completion with saved literal label time;
- light/medium/dark/null doneness choices;
- targeted doneness persistence preserving label facts and advancing `updatedAt`;
- completion remains open during enrichment;
- Done returns to fresh Capture;
- update failures (including rejection and not-found) preserve the created sighting;
- semantic controls, focus management, announced status/error feedback, and touch-sized buttons;
- route and PostgreSQL integration coverage for required behaviors.

No missing, partial, scope-creep, or incorrect-spec findings identified. Typecheck also passes.
